<UserControl
		xmlns="https://github.com/BobbyCannon/Cornerstone"
		xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
		xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
		xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
		xmlns:tabs="clr-namespace:Cornerstone.Sample.Tabs.AppDispatcher"
		mc:Ignorable="d" d:DesignWidth="660" d:DesignHeight="860"
		x:Class="Cornerstone.Sample.Tabs.AppDispatcher.TabAppDispatcherDemos"
		x:DataType="tabs:TabAppDispatcherDemos"
		x:Name="This">
	<ScrollViewer x:Name="PageScroll"
			HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
			VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
		<Grid x:Name="Layout" Margin="16,12,16,12" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*">
		<Grid.Styles>
			<Style Selector="SelectableTextBlock">
				<Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource ControlFontSize}" />
				<Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
				<Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{x:Static CornerstoneTheme.OpenSansLight}" />
			</Style>
		</Grid.Styles>
		<StackPanel x:Name="Intro" Grid.Row="0" Spacing="12">
			<SelectableTextBlock>
				<SelectableTextBlock.Text>
					Many MVVM apps forget to implement the M (Model) in MVVM. Many apps just work directly
					with the ViewModel meaning it is really just a VVM. The goal of the IAppDispatcher
					is to help assist with the Model to ViewModel updates.
				</SelectableTextBlock.Text>
			</SelectableTextBlock>
			<SelectableTextBlock>
				<SelectableTextBlock.Text>
					The Model can be updated Off Dispatcher on any thread. The AppDispatcher monitors
					the Model for updates. When there is an update, the AppDispatcher applies only
					the Model updates to the ViewModel On Dispatcher. The AppDispatcher is processed
					by the ApplicationViewModel on the provided worker delay.
				</SelectableTextBlock.Text>
			</SelectableTextBlock>
		</StackPanel>
		<StackPanel x:Name="Charts" Grid.Row="1" Margin="0,12,0,8" Spacing="8">
			<WrapPanel ItemSpacing="10"
					HorizontalAlignment="Center">
				<LineChart x:Name="ModelChart"
						Title="Model Updates"
						Data="{Binding GraphDataForModel}"
						Height="60"
						MaxWidth="360"
						HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" />
				<LineChart x:Name="ViewChart"
						Title="AppDispatcher Updates"
						Data="{Binding GraphDataForView}"
						Height="60"
						MaxWidth="360"
						HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" />
			</WrapPanel>
			<SelectableTextBlock>
				<SelectableTextBlock.Text>
					When the View is detached the ViewModel is marked as not attached. This disables
					any updates to the ViewModel even if the Model is updating Off Dispatcher. This
					allows for many DispatchableViewModels to be configured without much overhead.
					Switching tabs detaches that demo. This page stays up, so the charts keep recording.
				</SelectableTextBlock.Text>
			</SelectableTextBlock>
		</StackPanel>
		<TabControl Grid.Row="2">
			<TabItem Header="Automatic" Content="{Binding AutomaticView}" />
			<TabItem Header="Streaming" Content="{Binding StreamingView}" />
			<TabItem Header="Collections" Content="{Binding CollectionsView}" />
			<TabItem Header="Series" Content="{Binding SeriesView}" />
			<TabItem Header="Properties" Content="{Binding PropertiesView}" />
		</TabControl>
		</Grid>
	</ScrollViewer>
</UserControl>
